A replayed turn usually has reasoning *before* the calls (`reasoning, function_call, function_call`), not between them. Could we cover that order too, to make sure parallel calls after a reasoning item still merge into one turn?

```python
def test_extract_input_messages_reasoning_before_parallel_tool_calls(
    loaded_module,
):
    messages = loaded_module.get_input_messages(
        [
            {
                "id": "rs_1",
                "type": "reasoning",
                "summary": [{"type": "summary_text", "text": "Planning..."}],
            },
            {"type": "function_call", "call_id": "call_1", "name": "f1", "arguments": "{}"},
            {"type": "function_call", "call_id": "call_2", "name": "f2", "arguments": "{}"},
        ]
    )

    assert [m.role for m in messages] == ["assistant", "assistant"]
    assert [p.type for p in messages[0].parts] == ["reasoning"]
    assert [p.id for p in messages[1].parts] == ["call_1", "call_2"]
```
